<title>BELGIUM: CHANIC 1996 NET RISES TO 14.5 MLN BFR.</title>
<headline>CHANIC 1996 NET RISES TO 14.5 MLN BFR.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31,</p>
<p>1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit	    14.47  vs  13.74</p>
<p>    Cons extraordinary loss    0.76  vs   0.78</p>
<p>    Cons current profit	 15.24  vs  14.53</p>
<p>    Cons financial charges     6.22  vs  12.01</p>
<p>    Cons operating profit     21.46  vs  26.54</p>
<p>    Cons turnover/sales	788.13  vs 856.41</p>
<p>NOTE - Chanic SA is a Belgian holding company with various</p>
<p>activities and interests, principally in Africa. It is</p>
<p>controlled by holding company Finoutremer .</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said it would propose to</p>
<p>transfer 11.3 million francs of the profit to reserves and the</p>
<p>balance to attributable profit, bringing the accumulated loss</p>
<p>from previous years to 274.1 million francs.</p>
<p>&quot;In 1997, Chanic faces a particularly difficult year in</p>
<p>central Africa. The board hopes to achieve...positive current</p>
<p>earnings in line with those of 1996,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
